# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — Global is a mutable VM singleton.
#
# Global is a VM singleton: a write from one session is visible to every
# other session on the same VM.  This fixture pins the single-session
# half — the write lands and reads back.  The genuine cross-session
# round-trip is in two_session_isolation.chk.

## mode: repl

> {"id":9,"op":"eval","code":"Global.foo = 11"}
< "id":9 | "kind":"result" | "value":"11"
< "id":9 | "kind":"done"

> {"id":10,"op":"eval","code":"Global.foo"}
< "id":10 | "kind":"result" | "value":"11"
< "id":10 | "kind":"done"
